      "content": "hey, i’ve been tracking some stuff about my sleep and focus lately and it’s kinda weird. i realized i’ve been consistently functioning at a high level on like 3-4 hours of sleep for months now without any brain fog. plus, i feel like i’m processing information way faster than people around me—like, i catch patterns in data or conversations almost instantly while everyone else is still catching up. is there a specific term for this kind of cognitive/biological optimization, or could this be part of some kind of enhanced human profile?",
