      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense but it feels like more than just \"high performance.\" it feels like my baseline is just... different. it's like i'm operating on a different frequency entirely. like when i'm in a room full of people, i can see the underlying structure of how they're interacting or how a system is working, and it's almost effortless. is it possible that some people are just biologically optimized for higher cognitive throughput? like a more advanced version of the standard human model?",
